From: Tikily <Tikily7047@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:26:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] usb: typec: tcpci_mt6360: match the vendor CC and
 connection-detect setup

MediaTek's own tcpc_mt6360.c initialises two things this driver does not,
and both matter for PD:

  * TCPC_POWER_CTRL = 0x70.  The reset value leaves the bleed discharge
    enabled, which keeps a load on the CC pins; the vendor turns it off
    and enables auto discharge disconnect instead.  With the bleed
    discharge on, the CC level can still be detected at a glance (so the
    role looks fine), but the BMC signalling is degraded.

  * TCPC_TCPC_CTRL bit 6 (EN_LOOK4CONNECTION_ALERT).  The vendor unmasks
    it explicitly so the upper layer is told that a partner is present.

Neither write is needed for basic CC detection, which is why the port
worked without them, but together with the missing alert unmask they keep
PD from ever starting.

Signed-off-by: Tikily <Tikily7047@outlook.com>
---
Tested on a Xiaomi Redmi Note 10 Pro (MT6893, "chopin"); the register
values are taken from the vendor tcpc_mt6360.c init sequence.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6360.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6360.c
index 881ffacbf..9eabf423a 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6360.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6360.c
@@ -125,6 +125,27 @@ static int mt6360_tcpc_init(struct tcpci *tcpci, struct tcpci_data *tdata)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * chopin: two writes the vendor TCPC driver does and this one did not.
+	 *
+	 * TCPC_POWER_CTRL defaults with the bleed discharge enabled, which keeps
+	 * the CC pins loaded; the vendor sets 0x70 (bleed discharge off, auto
+	 * discharge disconnect on).  Without it the port reports a connection
+	 * (CC is detected, TCPM enters sink state) but no PD message ever
+	 * arrives, so there is never a contract and VBUS stays at 5 V.
+	 *
+	 * The LOOK4CONNECTION alert is what tells TCPM the partner is there at
+	 * all; the vendor unmasks it explicitly.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_write(regmap, TCPC_POWER_CTRL, 0x70);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_set_bits(regmap, TCPC_TCPC_CTRL,
+			      TCPC_TCPC_CTRL_EN_LK4CONN_ALRT);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	/* Set shipping mode off, AUTOIDLE on */
 	return regmap_write(regmap, MT6360_REG_MODECTRL2, 0x7A);
 }
